# Source for `npm run sync -- --source config/liberty-source.env` — copy this file to
# liberty-source.env (git-ignored) and fill it in. Values here override .env's MSSQL_*
# for that run only. The sync only ever SELECTs from Liberty.
#
# Clues from the restored backup's metadata (msdb restore history + RWD's own users,
# checked 2026-10-13):
#   - The shop's server is DESKTOP-ALTQTAR\LIBERTY  (machine DESKTOP-ALTQTAR, named
#     instance LIBERTY). Its backups were taken by `sa`, so that SQL login exists.
#   - RWD has three SQL users: `report` (db_datareader only — the one to use),
#     `appl` (reader + writer — almost certainly Liberty's own app login), and `seanb4`
#     (from 2000, likely the vendor's). Passwords aren't in the backup. Liberty's client
#     keeps its connection somewhere on the shop PC — check its install folder for an
#     .ini/.config, or an ODBC DSN (odbcad32.exe) — not verified.
#   - Easiest of all: run the sync *on* the shop PC as the Windows user that installed
#     Liberty, with Windows auth (no password), host localhost\LIBERTY.
#
# Reaching a named instance over the LAN needs SQL Server Configuration Manager >
# TCP/IP enabled for LIBERTY, the SQL Server Browser service running (UDP 1434), and the
# firewall open — or set a fixed port and use MSSQL_PORT. Alternatively take a fresh
# backup (Rwdback.7rbk), restore it locally as before, and point this at .\SQLEXPRESS.

# --- Option A: SQL login (works across the network)
MSSQL_HOST=DESKTOP-ALTQTAR\LIBERTY
MSSQL_DATABASE=RWD
MSSQL_USER=report
MSSQL_PASSWORD=
# MSSQL_PORT=1433          # only for a fixed-port instance; leave unset to use SQL Browser
MSSQL_ENCRYPT=false
MSSQL_TRUSTED_CONNECTION=false

# --- Option B: Windows auth (run on the shop PC itself)
# MSSQL_HOST=localhost\LIBERTY
# MSSQL_DATABASE=RWD
# MSSQL_TRUSTED_CONNECTION=true

# --- Target: the Teabox database to bring up to date. Stop teabox.exe first and back
# the file up (dist-bin/arch/). Forward slashes, real drive letter (root CLAUDE.md).
TEABOX_DATABASE_URL=file:C:/code/yetanotherteabox/dist-bin/teabox.db
